1
00:00:03,271 --> 00:00:07,621
On the night of 8 December 1980, John
Lennon came home to the Dakota,

2
00:00:07,641 --> 00:00:10,739
the apartment building on
Central Park West in New York.

3
00:00:12,621 --> 00:00:13,856
He was forty years old,

4
00:00:14,388 --> 00:00:16,928
and he was shot a few steps
from his own front door.

5
00:00:18,671 --> 00:00:22,640
This is what the record shows about
his last day, and about the days after.

6
00:00:27,121 --> 00:00:31,449
John Lennon was born in
Liverpool on 9 October 1940.

7
00:00:33,151 --> 00:00:35,607
The Beatles broke up in 1970,

8
00:00:35,858 --> 00:00:39,839
and in 1971 he moved to
New York with Yoko Ono.

9
00:00:41,621 --> 00:00:44,439
By 1973 they were living at the Dakota,

10
00:00:44,930 --> 00:00:47,728
a nineteenth century building
that faces Central Park.

11
00:00:49,711 --> 00:00:54,979
On 9 October 1975, his thirty-fifth
birthday, their son Sean was born.

12
00:00:56,861 --> 00:00:58,747
After that, Lennon stepped away

13
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:01,063
from the music business
for about five years,

14
00:01:01,314 --> 00:01:03,029
and stayed home to raise his son.

15
00:01:04,570 --> 00:01:14,800
For five years I've been so locked in the
home environment and completely switched
my way of thinking that I didn't really
think about music at all.

16
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:18,670
My guitar was sort of hung up behind the
bed, literally.

17
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:23,830
And he just sat up and said, You know what
I want to be when I grow up?

18
00:01:23,830 --> 00:01:28,220
And I said, no, what's that? He looked me
right in the eye and said, just a daddy.

19
00:01:29,771 --> 00:01:32,100
In June 1980, he took
Sean to Bermuda,

20
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:34,398
and there the songs began to come.

21
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:40,460
And I called her because I was in Bermuda
with Sean, and she was here in New York.

22
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:43,230
I said, well, look, we were talking about
recording.

23
00:01:43,230 --> 00:01:47,380
It must have triggered something off here,
because I'm getting all this stuff.

24
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:51,050
And I started singing it to her down the
phone or playing a cassette.

25
00:01:52,581 --> 00:01:55,613
From August to October they
recorded at the Hit Factory,

26
00:01:55,633 --> 00:01:57,188
a studio in New York.

27
00:01:59,092 --> 00:02:01,298
In September they signed
with Geffen Records.

28
00:02:02,941 --> 00:02:07,641
The album, Double Fantasy,
came out on 17 November 1980,

29
00:02:08,093 --> 00:02:10,729
and it was his first in
more than five years.

30
00:02:15,751 --> 00:02:17,636
On Saturday, 6 December,

31
00:02:17,656 --> 00:02:22,399
he gave a long interview to
Andy Peebles of BBC Radio One.

32
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:29,910
And it took me two years to unwind. I can
go out this door now and go in a
restaurant.

33
00:02:29,910 --> 00:02:33,990
Do you want to know how great that is? Or
go to the movies.

34
00:02:33,990 --> 00:02:39,660
I mean, people come up and ask for an
autograph or say hi, but they won't bug
you.

35
00:02:41,010 --> 00:02:45,610
He just seemed a very, very happy and very
involved person, and deeply in love with
his wife.

36
00:02:47,122 --> 00:02:49,628
Double Fantasy had been in
the shops for three weeks.

37
00:02:51,311 --> 00:02:54,071
Two days later, Monday, 8 December,

38
00:02:54,382 --> 00:02:56,299
was another working
day at the Dakota.

39
00:02:57,981 --> 00:02:58,953
In the afternoon,

40
00:02:59,003 --> 00:03:01,610
the photographer Annie
Leibovitz took pictures

41
00:03:01,630 --> 00:03:03,364
of Lennon and Ono in their apartment,

42
00:03:03,755 --> 00:03:05,429
and she left at half past three.

43
00:03:07,311 --> 00:03:09,910
Then a crew from RKO Radio arrived,

44
00:03:10,001 --> 00:03:12,539
and Lennon gave what
would be his last interview.

45
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:16,790
Because it's still up to us to make what
we can of it.

46
00:03:16,790 --> 00:03:19,500
It's not out of our control. I still
believe in love.

47
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,740
Peace. I still believe in positive
thinking.

48
00:03:23,090 --> 00:03:29,180
We all survived Vietnam, or Watergate, or
the tremendous upheaval of the whole world
that's changed.

49
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:33,750
We were the hip ones in the sixties, but
the world is not like the sixties.

50
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:37,660
The whole map's changed, and we're going
into an unknown future.

51
00:03:37,660 --> 00:03:41,190
But we're still all here. We're still
alive. There's hope.

52
00:03:42,721 --> 00:03:46,640
Around five o clock, the couple left for
the Record Plant, a recording studio,

53
00:03:46,991 --> 00:03:50,229
to work on a song of Ono's
called Walking on Thin Ice.

54
00:03:52,171 --> 00:03:52,803
At the door,

55
00:03:53,135 --> 00:03:55,262
a man who had been
waiting asked Lennon

56
00:03:55,282 --> 00:03:57,119
to sign a copy of Double Fantasy.

57
00:03:58,882 --> 00:04:00,847
Lennon signed it, and
they drove away.

58
00:04:02,511 --> 00:04:04,738
They worked in the studio
into the late evening,

59
00:04:04,758 --> 00:04:07,959
and at about ten fifty they
came back to the Dakota.

60
00:04:09,722 --> 00:04:11,748
Lennon planned to say
goodnight to his son.

61
00:04:13,411 --> 00:04:15,147
As they walked in
through the archway,

62
00:04:15,318 --> 00:04:17,978
the man who had asked for
the autograph was still there.

63
00:04:19,822 --> 00:04:21,968
He fired at Lennon
from a few feet away.

64
00:04:23,551 --> 00:04:25,970
Police officers arrived
about two minutes later,

65
00:04:26,182 --> 00:04:28,159
and arrested the gunman on the spot.

66
00:04:29,721 --> 00:04:33,648
Two officers drove Lennon to
Roosevelt Hospital in their patrol car.

67
00:04:35,411 --> 00:04:38,791
His death certificate gives the
time of death as eleven fifteen,

68
00:04:39,263 --> 00:04:41,580
though another time
has also been reported.

69
00:04:46,142 --> 00:04:49,129
That night, Monday Night Football
was on American television.

70
00:04:50,691 --> 00:04:51,514
During the game,

71
00:04:51,534 --> 00:04:54,875
Howard Cosell told the viewers
that Lennon was dead on arrival,

72
00:04:55,166 --> 00:04:56,340
and then the game went on.

73
00:04:57,941 --> 00:05:00,642
Outside the Dakota, people
began to gather that night,

74
00:05:00,673 --> 00:05:02,249
and they kept coming all night.

75
00:05:03,912 --> 00:05:06,838
The next day, Yoko Ono said
that there would be no funeral.

76
00:05:08,501 --> 00:05:11,882
Her statement ended, John loved
and prayed for the human race.

77
00:05:12,354 --> 00:05:13,949
Please pray the same for him.

78
00:05:15,671 --> 00:05:18,821
Paul McCartney, speaking to
reporters outside his home in Sussex,

79
00:05:18,841 --> 00:05:21,058
said, I can't take it at the moment.

80
00:05:22,941 --> 00:05:26,561
George Harrison said in a statement,
After all we went through together,

81
00:05:26,651 --> 00:05:29,529
I had and still have great
love and respect for him.

82
00:05:31,171 --> 00:05:33,268
Ringo Starr, who was in the Bahamas,

83
00:05:33,579 --> 00:05:36,359
flew to New York to
console Ono and Sean.

84
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:43,330
Well, by the standards of great musicians,
he wasn't a great musician, but he was a
great man.

85
00:05:43,330 --> 00:05:46,320
I mean, he was one of the originals of
this century.

86
00:05:47,871 --> 00:05:51,491
Lennon was cremated on 9
December at Ferncliff cemetery,

87
00:05:51,743 --> 00:05:53,999
and his ashes were
scattered in Central Park.

88
00:05:55,721 --> 00:05:56,744
Instead of a funeral,

89
00:05:56,764 --> 00:06:01,849
Ono asked for ten minutes of
silence, on Sunday 14 December.

90
00:06:03,671 --> 00:06:04,624
In Central Park,

91
00:06:04,935 --> 00:06:07,504
estimates of the crowd
run from fifty thousand

92
00:06:07,524 --> 00:06:09,139
to more than a hundred thousand.

93
00:06:10,841 --> 00:06:13,030
In Liverpool, reports of the crowd run

94
00:06:13,050 --> 00:06:15,269
from fifteen thousand
to thirty thousand.

95
00:06:16,871 --> 00:06:20,197
Radio stations in New York went
off the air for those ten minutes.

96
00:06:22,182 --> 00:06:24,967
In San Diego, people
gathered in Balboa Park.

97
00:06:26,610 --> 00:06:31,080
It's not what he said twenty years ago,
because he was where you were twenty years
ago.

98
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:35,200
It's what he said in 1980. And what he was
saying, and wanting to say, was hope.

99
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:37,460
And he was wanting to say, love your
family.

100
00:06:38,951 --> 00:06:40,366
And at a record store there,

101
00:06:40,477 --> 00:06:43,359
Double Fantasy had sold
out the day after his death.

102
00:06:45,001 --> 00:06:48,190
It had been on sale at five
dollars ninety nine cents,

103
00:06:48,210 --> 00:06:51,209
and when it was restocked,
the price was six ninety nine.

104
00:06:56,031 --> 00:06:58,629
The gunman pleaded guilty
to second degree murder,

105
00:06:59,001 --> 00:07:01,399
against his lawyers'
advice to plead insanity.

106
00:07:03,161 --> 00:07:06,688
In 1981 he was sentenced
to twenty years to life.

107
00:07:08,531 --> 00:07:11,389
He became eligible for
parole in the year 2000,

108
00:07:11,721 --> 00:07:14,359
and has been denied it
at least fourteen times.

109
00:07:16,221 --> 00:07:17,716
At the next Grammy Awards,

110
00:07:18,028 --> 00:07:20,808
Double Fantasy won the
Grammy for Album of the Year.

111
00:07:22,691 --> 00:07:27,400
On 9 October 1985, what would have
been Lennon's forty-fifth birthday,

112
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:31,919
New York dedicated a memorial in
Central Park, across from the Dakota.

113
00:07:33,821 --> 00:07:35,284
It is called Strawberry Fields.

114
00:07:35,304 --> 00:07:39,562
Ono and the mayor,
Ed Koch, dedicated it,

115
00:07:39,974 --> 00:07:42,869
and Ono gave more than a
million dollars toward its upkeep.

116
00:07:44,592 --> 00:07:47,779
Every year, on 8 December,
fans gather there.

117
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:53,760
And I consider that my work won't be
finished until I'm dead and buried, and I
hope that's a long, long time.

118
00:07:55,232 --> 00:07:57,378
He had been back at work
for only a few months.

119
00:07:59,043 --> 00:08:00,386
What would he have made next?
